# Sample isolation

This repo is a collection of **independent** Android Architecture Components samples. Each top-level directory (`BasicSample`, `GithubBrowserSample`, `PagingSample`, etc.) is its own Gradle project.

- Change only the sample that is in scope. Do not "improve" other samples in the same PR.
- Match that sample's language and stack. Java samples stay Java; Kotlin samples stay Kotlin. Do not introduce Compose, Hilt, or Navigation into a sample that does not already use them.
- Treat samples as teaching code for a specific API (Room, LiveData, Paging, WorkManager, Navigation, ViewBinding). Prefer the same patterns already used in that sample over newer alternatives.

# File headers and style

New source files need the Apache 2.0 Android Open Source Project copyright header used by neighboring files.

```java
// ❌ BAD — missing header, mixed style
class Foo { }

// ✅ GOOD — match the sample's existing header year format and code style
/*
 * Copyright (C) 2017 The Android Open Source Project
 * ... Apache 2.0 license block ...
 */
```

Follow the existing style in the target sample ([Android Code Style Guide](https://source.android.com/source/code-style.html)). Java samples often use `m` prefixes; Kotlin samples do not.

# Issues

This repo tracks **sample** bugs. Architecture Components library bugs belong on the [issuetracker](https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/new?component=197448&template=878802).
